:"suspicious","score":26,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789018113886},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill only provides reasoning-persona instructions, with no code execution or data access, though users should know it may change the assistant's tone or critique style automatically.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill does not request filesystem, network, credential, tool, or account access, so its environment impact is proportionate to a reasoning aid.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact contains Markdown files only, with no scripts, dependencies, remote fetches, installer logic, or executable components.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The activation language is broad and permits silent operation, so a user may not always see when a persona is shaping the response.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanism, background process, privilege change, memory write, hook, or profile/session access was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to apply reasoning personas for brainstorming, review, decisions, and architecture analysis; the artifact contents match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this if you want the assistant to apply stronger critique, precedent-checking, or integration-focused reasoning. Be aware that it may activate from broad contexts like brainstorming, code review, or architecture decisions, and it may not always label the active persona unless your agent or workflow requires disclosure.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad activation terms are real, but they are part of the disclosed purpose of a persona-selection skill and do not create external authority or hidden data access.\n[SQP-1] expected: The auto-activation map could cause unexpected tone changes in generic brainstorming or review contexts, but the behavior is visible in the artifact and limited to response framing.\n[SQP-2] expected: The skill explicitly allows persona use without a marker, which is a transparency caveat rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SQP-1] expected: The referenced persona details provide prompts and question sets without separate exclusion rules; this is a scope-quality issue, not a security hold by itself.\n[SQP-1] expected: Conversational activation wording may be imprecise, but there is no artifact-backed instruction to bypass safety rules, execute tools, access data, or persist changes.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789018113886}}}}}